#: src/macros/macro_rules/repetition.md:6
msgid "Repetition"
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/macro_rules/repetition.md:8
msgid ""
"Declarative macros can match and expand lists of items of arbitrary length. "
"This is defined using the repetition syntax on both the left and right sides "
"of the match rules:"
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/macro_rules/repetition.md:12
msgid "`$( ... ) SEPARATOR OPERATOR`"
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/macro_rules/repetition.md:14
msgid ""
"**Separator:** An optional token separating each matched item (typically `,` "
"or `;`)."
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/macro_rules/repetition.md:16
msgid "**Operators:**"
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/macro_rules/repetition.md:17
msgid "`*`: Match zero or more repetitions."
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/macro_rules/repetition.md:18
msgid "`+`: Match one or more repetitions."
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/macro_rules/repetition.md:19
msgid "`?`: Match zero or one (optional)."
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/macro_rules/repetition.md:22
msgid "// Copyright 2026 Google LLC\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/macro_rules/repetition.md:23
msgid "// SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/macro_rules/repetition.md:26
msgid "// Match one or more expressions separated by commas:\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/macro_rules/repetition.md:28
msgid "// Expand the repetition:\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/macro_rules/repetition.md:30
msgid "\"Value: {}\""
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/macro_rules/repetition.md:36
msgid "\"hello\""
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/macro_rules/repetition.md:42
msgid ""
"Explain that the repetition block on the right-hand side `$( ... )*` must "
"contain the exact meta-variables defined inside the left-hand side's "
"repetition block."
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/macro_rules/repetition.md:45
msgid ""
"Note that the separator on the left-hand side (the comma `,` in `$"
"( $val:expr ),+`), which is used to parse the input stream, may differ from "
"that used on the right-hand side to join elements in the output stream. "
"Here, the output separator is empty, resulting in sequential statements."
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/macro_rules/repetition.md:49
msgid "You can use any punctuation token (except delimiters) as a separator."
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/macro_rules/repetition.md:50
msgid ""
"Most syntactic constructs in Rust itself accept separators as terminators as "
"well. To allow a trailing separator with repetition syntax, an optional "
"separator may be accepted explicitly after a `*` or `+` repetition operator: "
"`$($e:expr),+ $(,)?`"
msgstr ""
